{
  "id": "04607_abaku",
  "headword": "{暴|あば}く",
  "reading": "あばく",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to expose; to reveal; to unmask",
  "conjugation": {
    "type": "godan",
    "ending": "く",
    "stem": "{暴|あば}"
  },
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to expose; to reveal; to unmask",
      "explanation": "To bring hidden wrongdoing, secrets, or lies to light."
    },
    {
      "sense_number": 2,
      "gloss": "to dig up; to exhume",
      "explanation": "To disturb or open something that was buried or concealed."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "04607_abaku_ex1",
      "japanese": "{不正|ふせい}を{暴|あば}く。",
      "english": "To expose corruption.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "04607_abaku_ex2",
      "japanese": "{嘘|うそ}を{暴|あば}かれて、{彼|かれ}は{黙|だま}り{込|こ}んだ。",
      "english": "When his lies were exposed, he fell silent.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "04607_abaku_ex3",
      "japanese": "{記者|きしゃ}が{政治家|せいじか}の{不正|ふせい}を{暴|あば}いた。",
      "english": "The journalist exposed the politician's corruption.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "04607_abaku_ex4",
      "japanese": "{墓|はか}を{暴|あば}く。",
      "english": "To dig up a grave.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "04607_abaku_ex5",
      "japanese": "{盗掘者|とうくつしゃ}が{古墳|こふん}を{暴|あば}いた。",
      "english": "Grave robbers dug up the ancient tomb.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "04607_abaku_ex6",
      "japanese": "{考古学者|こうこがくしゃ}たちは{遺跡|いせき}を{暴|あば}いて{貴重|きちょう}な{土器|どき}を{発見|はっけん}した。",
      "english": "The archaeologists unearthed the ruins and discovered precious pottery.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "{暴|あば}く is a transitive verb ({他動詞|たどうし}). The intransitive counterpart is {暴|あば}かれる (passive: to be exposed).\n\nASPECT ({ている}):\n{暴|あば}いている indicates an ongoing process of exposing something.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {不正|ふせい}を{暴|あば}く - to expose corruption\n- {嘘|うそ}を{暴|あば}く - to unmask lies\n- {真実|しんじつ}を{暴|あば}く - to reveal the truth\n- {秘密|ひみつ}を{暴|あば}く - to expose a secret\n- {正体|しょうたい}を{暴|あば}く - to unmask someone's true identity\n\nNUANCE:\nThis verb is typically used in serious contexts involving wrongdoing or hidden truths. It carries a sense of forcefully bringing something shameful or secret into the open.",
